---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Soul That Drinks — Daf Yomi Game: Chullin 120"
  description="Chullin 120: work the alchemist's bench. Congeal the blood, melt the forbidden fat, dissolve the chametz on Pesach, liquefy a bird carcass over fire and over sun — then stamp the verdict. Three times Reish Lakish reads 'soul' to include the one who drinks, and the Gemara spends the daf blocking every shortcut derivation. Find the stringency that blocks each one, forge the one pair that works, and swing the two exegetical lenses of Rabbi Eliezer and Rabbi Yehoshua."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,500;9..144,700;9..144,900&family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[#08120e] !text-[#dfe8dd]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <div class="border-b border-[#1e3a30] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#0e1f19] to-transparent px-4 pt-10 pb-8 text-center">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] !text-[#e8ae3c]">
        <a href="/daf" class="hover:!text-[#ffc95e]">daf yomi arcade</a> · chullin 120 · 2026-08-28
      </p>
      <h1 class="fraunces text-4xl font-black tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">⚗️ The Soul That Drinks</h1>
      <p class="frank mt-2 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#e8ae3c]" dir="rtl" lang="he">״נֶפֶשׁ״ — לְרַבּוֹת אֶת הַשּׁוֹתֶה</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-1 text-xs italic !text-[#8fa898]">"Soul — to include the one who drinks." Reish Lakish's answer, three times on this daf.</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#b8c9bc]">
        On Chullin 120 everything changes state. Fat melts, bread dissolves, blood congeals, a
        carcass liquefies over fire — or rots in the sun. The Torah says <i>eat</i>; these people
        <i>drank</i>. Does the law follow the substance into its new form? Work the bench and stamp
        each verdict. Then step up to the forge, where the Gemara blocks derivation after
        derivation — and your job is to find the stringency doing the blocking.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-16 pt-8">
      <!-- ============ Score strip ============ -->
      <div class="sticky top-2 z-20 mb-8 rounded-2xl border border-[#1e3a30] bg-[#0c1a15]/95 px-4 py-2.5 text-center shadow-lg shadow-black/40 backdrop-blur">
        <span class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#8fa898]">first-try verdicts</span>
        <span id="score" class="fraunces ml-2 text-base font-bold !text-[#e8ae3c]">0 / 13</span>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Act I: The Bench ============ -->
      <section aria-labelledby="act1-h">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] !text-[#5ecfb4]">act i · the bench</p>
        <h2 id="act1-h" class="fraunces mt-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#dfe8dd]">Change the state, stamp the verdict</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#b8c9bc]">
          Eight substances from the daf. Run the process the case describes — watch the flask —
          then choose the ruling the Gemara actually gives.
        </p>
        <div id="bench" class="mt-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Act II: The Forge ============ -->
      <section aria-labelledby="act2-h" class="mt-12">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] !text-[#5ecfb4]">act ii · the refutation forge</p>
        <h2 id="act2-h" class="fraunces mt-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#dfe8dd]">Why did the Torah write it three times?</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#b8c9bc]">
          "Soul" appears by forbidden fat, by chametz, and by the bird carcass. The Gemara asks:
          drop one verse and derive it from the others! Each attempt is blocked by a
          stringency the sources share but the target lacks. You find the blocker.
        </p>
        <div id="forge" class="mt-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Act III: The Lenses ============ -->
      <section aria-labelledby="act3-h" class="mt-12">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] !text-[#5ecfb4]">act iii · the two lenses</p>
        <h2 id="act3-h" class="fraunces mt-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#dfe8dd]">Rabbi Eliezer vs. Rabbi Yehoshua</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#b8c9bc]">
          Teruma's liquid-law is derived from first fruits. But how much of the source case comes
          along with the derivation? Swing the lens and watch three real verdicts flip.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose an exegetical method">
          <button id="lens-e" role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="lens-tab rounded-xl border px-3 py-3 text-left transition">
            <span class="block text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide">Rabbi Eliezer</span>
            <span class="frank block text-lg font-bold" dir="rtl" lang="he">דּוּן מִינַּהּ וּמִינַּהּ</span>
            <span class="block text-[11px]">Infer from it — and again from it: the whole source case comes along.</span>
          </button>
          <button id="lens-y" role="tab" aria-selected="true" class="lens-tab rounded-xl border px-3 py-3 text-left transition">
            <span class="block text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide">Rabbi Yehoshua</span>
            <span class="frank block text-lg font-bold" dir="rtl" lang="he">דּוּן מִינַּהּ וְאוֹקֵי בְאַתְרַהּ</span>
            <span class="block text-[11px]">Infer from it — but interpret it in its own place: only the principle transfers.</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <div id="lens-cards" class="mt-3 space-y-3" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Final grade ============ -->
      <div id="finale" class="mt-12 hidden rounded-2xl border border-[#e8ae3c]/40 bg-[#141d12] p-6 text-center"></div>

      <!-- ============ Learn the real daf ============ -->
      <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl border border-[#1e3a30] bg-[#0c1a15] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#e8ae3c]">learn the real daf</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#b8c9bc]">
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#dfe8dd]">The opener you didn't play:</b> can a hair count as "protection" for flesh when it rides on
            top of the hide — protection upon protection? Rabbi Yoḥanan says the hair pierces the hide and touches the flesh.
            Rav Aḥa objects: if hides are full of perforations, how do we ever write valid tefillin? Answer, from Eretz
            Yisrael: any hole the ink covers is not a hole
            (<a class="!text-[#e8ae3c] underline hover:!text-[#ffc95e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.120a.2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">120a:2–5</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#dfe8dd]">What are rotev and kifa?</b> After Abaye's objections: <i>rotev</i> is fat that oozed from
            the meat and congealed — not eaten itself, but it joins the meat toward an egg-bulk for food impurity. <i>Kifa</i>,
            per Rav Pappa, is the spices
            (<a class="!text-[#e8ae3c] underline hover:!text-[#ffc95e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.120a.9" target="_blank" rel="noopener">120a:9–15</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#dfe8dd]">The chain for consecrated produce:</b> tevel, chadash, shemitta produce, and kilayim
            arise on their own — but hekdesh needs a person's act of consecration, so its liquid-law needs a source:
            bikkurim is blocked, teruma is blocked, the two together are blocked, until teruma-plus-one-of-the-drinks forges
            (<a class="!text-[#e8ae3c] underline hover:!text-[#ffc95e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.120b.3" target="_blank" rel="noopener">120b:3–13</a>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <b class="!text-[#dfe8dd]">Go deeper:</b>
            <a class="!text-[#e8ae3c] underline hover:!text-[#ffc95e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.120a" target="_blank" rel="noopener">read Chullin 120 on Sefaria</a>
            with its most-linked commentaries: Steinsaltz (55 links), Rashi (44), Tosafot (17), and Chidushei Chatam Sofer (15).
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-center text-[11px] !text-[#5d7365]">
        <a href="/daf" class="underline hover:!text-[#8fa898]">← back to the daf yomi arcade</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style is:global>
    .fraunces { font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif; }
    .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', serif; }
    .lens-tab { border-color: #1e3a30; background: #0c1a15; color: #8fa898 !important; }
    .lens-tab span { color: inherit !important; }
    .lens-tab[aria-selected='true'] { border-color: #e8ae3c; background: #17211a; color: #e8ae3c !important; }
    .lens-tab:focus-visible, button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #5ecfb4; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .flask-liquid, .flask-chunk { transition: all 1.1s ease; }
    .verdict-btn { transition: background 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      *, .flask-liquid, .flask-chunk { transition: none !important; animation: none !important; }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    // ---------- palette helpers (global.css forces dark text colors; every color needs !important) ----------
    const C = {
      text: '!text-[#dfe8dd]', dim: '!text-[#b8c9bc]', mute: '!text-[#8fa898]',
      amber: '!text-[#e8ae3c]', teal: '!text-[#5ecfb4]', red: '!text-[#e2604f]',
    };
    const sef = (ref, label) =>
      `<a class="${C.amber} underline hover:!text-[#ffc95e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/${ref}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">${label}</a>`;

    // ---------- flask ----------
    // state: { lvl: 0..1 liquid fill, color, chunk: bool, chunkColor, murky: bool }
    let flaskN = 0;
    function flaskSVG(state) {
      const id = 'fc' + flaskN++;
      const H = 128, top = 6;
      const lh = Math.round(state.lvl * 76);
      const shape = 'M52 6 L52 50 L24 114 Q19 126 30 126 L90 126 Q101 126 96 114 L68 50 L68 6 Z';
      return `
      <svg viewBox="0 0 120 132" class="h-32 w-28 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true">
        <defs><clipPath id="${id}"><path d="${shape}"/></clipPath></defs>
        <g clip-path="url(#${id})">
          <rect class="flask-liquid" x="0" width="120" y="${H - 2 - lh}" height="${lh + 2}"
            fill="${state.color}" opacity="${state.murky ? 0.65 : 0.85}"></rect>
          <rect class="flask-chunk" x="42" width="36" rx="7"
            y="${state.chunk ? 92 : 126}" height="${state.chunk ? 32 : 0}"
            fill="${state.chunkColor || '#c9a06a'}" opacity="${state.chunk ? 1 : 0}"></rect>
        </g>
        <path d="${shape}" fill="none" stroke="#5ecfb4" stroke-opacity="0.6" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
        <line x1="46" y1="6" x2="74" y2="6" stroke="#5ecfb4" stroke-opacity="0.6" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"></line>
      </svg>`;
    }
    function setFlask(el, state) {
      const H = 128, lh = Math.round(state.lvl * 76);
      const liq = el.querySelector('.flask-liquid'), ch = el.querySelector('.flask-chunk');
      liq.setAttribute('y', H - 2 - lh); liq.setAttribute('height', lh + 2);
      liq.setAttribute('fill', state.color); liq.setAttribute('opacity', state.murky ? 0.65 : 0.85);
      ch.setAttribute('y', state.chunk ? 92 : 126); ch.setAttribute('height', state.chunk ? 32 : 0);
      ch.setAttribute('opacity', state.chunk ? 1 : 0);
      if (state.chunkColor) ch.setAttribute('fill', state.chunkColor);
    }

    // ---------- Act I data ----------
    const BENCH = [
      {
        name: 'Fat on the soup', he: 'רוֹטֶב',
        pre: { lvl: 0.42, color: '#8a5a2b', chunk: true, chunkColor: '#7a4b22' }, post: { lvl: 0.55, color: '#e8ae3c', chunk: true, chunkColor: '#7a4b22', murky: true },
        process: '🥣 Ladle liquid fat over the meat',
        scenario: 'Meat sits in the flask, short of an egg-bulk. Liquid fat floats on the soup around it. Together they reach an egg-bulk — do they join to impart the impurity of food?',
        options: [
          'Yes — like brine on a vegetable, which joins toward the Yom Kippur measure',
          'No — a liquid and a solid have different measures and never join for impurity',
          'Only if the fat came from that same piece of meat',
        ],
        correct: 1,
        reveal: `<b class="${C.red}">They do not join.</b> Impurity needs partners with a common measure, and liquid foods and solid foods measure differently. Yom Kippur is the exception that proves it: there the Torah cares only about affliction — anything that settles the mind counts — so Reish Lakish lets brine join a vegetable toward the date-bulk. Congealed fat, though, joins the meat: that is the mishna's <i>rotev</i>.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.120a.11', refLabel: 'Chullin 120a:11–13',
      },
      {
        name: 'Blood', he: 'דָּם',
        pre: { lvl: 0.5, color: '#a02020', chunk: false }, post: { lvl: 0.12, color: '#6a1414', chunk: true, chunkColor: '#5c1010' },
        process: '🧊 Congeal it and eat',
        scenario: 'Blood is drunk, not eaten — and the eating-prohibition says "eat." One congealed blood into a solid mass and ate it.',
        options: [
          'Exempt — blood is not normally eaten this way',
          'Liable — by congealing it he ascribed to it the significance of food',
          'Liable only if he ate an egg-bulk',
        ],
        correct: 1,
        reveal: `<b class="${C.amber}">Liable.</b> Congealing it was itself the act of making it food: he gave the blood the significance of eating, and the Torah says "You shall eat neither fat nor blood" (Leviticus 3:17).`,
        ref: 'Chullin.120a.16', refLabel: 'Chullin 120a:16–17',
      },
      {
        name: 'Forbidden fat', he: 'חֵלֶב',
        pre: { lvl: 0.06, color: '#e8ae3c', chunk: true, chunkColor: '#e6d9a8' }, post: { lvl: 0.5, color: '#e8ae3c', chunk: false },
        process: '🔥 Melt it over the fire and drink',
        scenario: 'The Torah writes eating by forbidden fat: "You shall eat no fat of ox or sheep or goat." One melted the cheilev and swallowed it as a liquid — drinking, not eating.',
        options: [
          'Exempt — the Torah said eating, and drinking is not eating',
          'Liable rabbinically only',
          'Liable — "the soul that eats it" (Leviticus 7:25) includes the one who drinks',
        ],
        correct: 2,
        reveal: `<b class="${C.amber}">Liable.</b> Reish Lakish: the verse says "the <i>soul</i> that eats it shall be cut off" — and "soul" comes to include the drinker. First of three times this move saves the daf.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.120a.18', refLabel: 'Chullin 120a:17–18',
      },
      {
        name: 'Chametz', he: 'חָמֵץ',
        pre: { lvl: 0.28, color: '#7fb8c9', chunk: true, chunkColor: '#c9a06a' }, post: { lvl: 0.55, color: '#b99b62', chunk: false, murky: true },
        process: '💧 Dissolve the bread in water and swallow — on Pesach',
        scenario: 'One took leavened bread, dissolved it fully in water, and swallowed the mixture during Pesach. "Eating" is what the Torah forbade.',
        options: [
          'Karet — "all who eat… that soul shall be cut off" (Exodus 12:15) includes the drinker',
          'Exempt from karet — he drank, he did not eat',
          'Lashes, but not karet',
        ],
        correct: 0,
        reveal: `<b class="${C.red}">Karet.</b> Reish Lakish again: "soul" — to include the one who drinks. The dissolved bread is still chametz to the Torah.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.120a.21', refLabel: 'Chullin 120a:19–21',
      },
      {
        name: 'Matza', he: 'מַצָּה',
        pre: { lvl: 0.28, color: '#7fb8c9', chunk: true, chunkColor: '#e6d9a8' }, post: { lvl: 0.55, color: '#cbbf94', chunk: false, murky: true },
        process: '💧 Dissolve the matza in water and swallow — seder night',
        scenario: 'Same trick, mirror case: matza dissolved in water and swallowed on the first night of Pesach. Has he fulfilled the mitzva of eating matza?',
        options: [
          'Yes — if chametz counts for karet, matza counts for the mitzva',
          'Yes, but only after the fact',
          'No — the Torah requires "the bread of affliction," and this is no longer bread',
        ],
        correct: 2,
        reveal: `<b class="${C.red}">Not fulfilled.</b> The inclusion of "soul" works for the prohibition, but the mitzva has its own words: "seven days you shall eat… the bread of affliction" (Deuteronomy 16:3). Dissolved matza is not <i>lechem oni</i>. Stringent on both sides.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.120a.19', refLabel: 'Chullin 120a:19–20',
      },
      {
        name: 'Bird carcass', he: 'נִבְלַת עוֹף טָהוֹר',
        pre: { lvl: 0.06, color: '#b98b62', chunk: true, chunkColor: '#a4785a' }, post: { lvl: 0.5, color: '#b98b62', chunk: false },
        process: '🔥 Liquefy it over the fire and drink',
        scenario: 'The carcass of a kosher bird makes its eater impure — "every soul that eats a carcass… shall be impure" (Leviticus 17:15). One liquefied it over fire and drank it.',
        options: [
          'Pure — impurity through eating requires eating',
          'Impure — "every soul" includes the one who drinks',
          'Impure only if it congeals again inside him',
        ],
        correct: 1,
        reveal: `<b class="${C.amber}">Impure.</b> Third appearance of the refrain: "every <i>soul</i>" — to include the drinker. Fire-melted carcass is still carcass.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.120a.22', refLabel: 'Chullin 120a:22–23',
      },
      {
        name: 'Carcass in the sun', he: 'חַמָּה',
        pre: { lvl: 0.06, color: '#b98b62', chunk: true, chunkColor: '#a4785a' }, post: { lvl: 0.45, color: '#6f7d3c', chunk: false, murky: true },
        process: '☀️ Leave it to melt in the sun, then drink',
        scenario: 'Same bird carcass — but this one was left to liquefy slowly in the sun before being drunk. Same "every soul"?',
        options: [
          'Impure — what difference does the heat source make?',
          'Impure, but only rabbinically',
          'Pure — the sun is slow: it rots before it melts, and rot is not food',
        ],
        correct: 2,
        reveal: `<b class="${C.teal}">Pure.</b> The sun takes so long that the carcass putrefies on the way — mere spoiled matter, unfit for any consumption, is no longer "eaten" at all. The heat source is really a time source.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.120a.23', refLabel: 'Chullin 120a:22–23',
      },
      {
        name: 'Creeping-animal gravy', he: 'שְׁרָצִים',
        pre: { lvl: 0.1, color: '#5b7d3c', chunk: true, chunkColor: '#4a6332' }, post: { lvl: 0.4, color: '#5b7d3c', chunk: false, murky: true },
        process: '🍲 Cook it down to juice, gravy, and sediment',
        scenario: 'The Sages read the letter heh in "hatteme\'im" (Leviticus 11:31) to forbid the juice, gravy, and flesh-sediments of creeping animals. How much must one consume to be liable?',
        options: [
          'An olive-bulk, like melted fat and dissolved chametz',
          'A lentil-bulk — the tiny measure of the creeping animal itself',
          'Any amount at all',
        ],
        correct: 1,
        reveal: `<b class="${C.amber}">A lentil-bulk.</b> That is exactly why the verse could not be skipped: derived from the other cases, <i>dayo</i> would cap liability at their olive-bulk. The heh teaches that the liquid follows the sheretz's own famously tiny measure.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.120a.33', refLabel: 'Chullin 120a:33–34',
      },
    ];

    // ---------- Act II data ----------
    const FORGE = [
      {
        title: 'Erase the verse by the bird carcass',
        setup: 'Let the Torah not write "every soul" by the carcass — derive drinking-impurity from <b>melted fat + dissolved chametz</b>.',
        options: [
          'Both are punishable by karet — the carcass-eater is not',
          'Both had no period of fitness',
          'Both impart impurity to the one who eats them',
        ],
        correct: 0,
        reveal: `<b class="${C.teal}">Blocked.</b> What is notable about fat and chametz? Karet. Eating a carcass carries no karet — so the target is lighter than everything the sources share, and the derivation dies. The carcass needs its own "soul."`,
        ref: 'Chullin.120a.27', refLabel: 'Chullin 120a:24–27',
      },
      {
        title: 'Erase the verse by chametz',
        setup: 'Let the Torah not write "soul" by chametz — derive drinking-karet from <b>melted fat + the carcass</b>.',
        options: [
          'Both are punishable by karet',
          'Both never had a period of fitness — but chametz was permitted before Pesach',
          'Both come from animals',
        ],
        correct: 1,
        reveal: `<b class="${C.teal}">Blocked.</b> Forbidden fat was never permitted to its eater; a carcass was never fit. Chametz, though, sat on the table perfectly kosher until Pesach began. The sources share a stringency chametz lacks.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.120a.28', refLabel: 'Chullin 120a:28',
      },
      {
        title: 'Erase the verse by forbidden fat',
        setup: 'Let the Torah not write "soul" by cheilev — derive drinking-liability from <b>chametz + the carcass</b>.',
        options: [
          'Both are forbidden in any amount',
          'Both are forbidden only to Israelites',
          'Neither has any permitted counterpart — but cheilev of a wild animal is permitted',
        ],
        correct: 2,
        reveal: `<b class="${C.teal}">Blocked.</b> Chametz on Pesach and carcass-meat have no permitted version. Cheilev does: the same fat in a <i>chayah</i> is permitted. (And the bird sin-offering eaten by priests? That doesn't count — the priests receive it "from the table of the Most High.")`,
        ref: 'Chullin.120a.29', refLabel: 'Chullin 120a:29–32',
      },
      {
        title: 'Erase the heh of "hatteme\'im"',
        setup: 'Creeping-animal juice and gravy — surely derivable from all three "soul" cases. Why must the Torah still write it?',
        options: [
          'Creeping animals are not food, so no derivation could start',
          'Dayo — a derived law cannot exceed its sources, and they only forbid an olive-bulk; the verse teaches a lentil-bulk',
          'Juice is not gravy, and gravy is not sediment',
        ],
        correct: 1,
        reveal: `<b class="${C.teal}">Needed.</b> The derivation would work — and that is the problem. <i>Dayo</i>: the conclusion can be no stronger than its source, which would mean olive-bulk liability. The heh writes the sheretz's lentil-bulk into its gravy.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.120a.34', refLabel: 'Chullin 120a:33–34',
      },
      {
        title: 'Reverse the flow',
        setup: 'Then flip it: write only the creeping-animal verse, and derive fat, chametz, and carcass <b>from the sheretz</b>.',
        options: [
          'Creeping animals impart impurity in any amount — the others need an olive-bulk',
          'Creeping animals are not drunk',
          'The sheretz verse is about impurity, not prohibition',
        ],
        correct: 0,
        reveal: `<b class="${C.teal}">Blocked both ways.</b> The sheretz is the strictest of all — a lentil-bulk, where the others demand an olive-bulk. A source stricter than its targets proves nothing about them. Four verses, all necessary.`,
        ref: 'Chullin.120b.2', refLabel: 'Chullin 120b:1–2',
      },
    ];

    // Forge finale: pick the valid pair for hekdesh
    const PAIR_CARDS = [
      { id: 'bik', name: 'First fruits', he: 'בִּכּוּרִים', note: 'liquid = fruit (wine may be brought)' },
      { id: 'ter', name: 'Teruma', he: 'תְּרוּמָה', note: 'liquid = produce, via bikkurim' },
      { id: 'cham', name: 'Dissolved chametz', he: 'חָמֵץ', note: '"soul" includes the drinker' },
      { id: 'carc', name: 'Melted carcass', he: 'נְבֵלָה', note: '"every soul" includes the drinker' },
    ];
    const PAIR_VERDICTS = {
      'bik|ter': { ok: false, why: 'Blocked: both carry death at the hand of Heaven and the added fifth for a non-priest — consecrated produce carries neither.' },
      'cham|carc': { ok: false, why: 'Blocked: both prohibitions arise on their own — hekdesh exists only after a person consecrates it.' },
      'bik|cham': { ok: true, why: 'Forged! Each partner cancels the other\'s stringency: chametz answers the death-and-fifth of bikkurim; bikkurim answers chametz\'s arising-on-its-own. The shared core — the liquid is like the source — transfers to hekdesh.' },
      'bik|carc': { ok: true, why: 'Forged! The carcass cancels bikkurim\'s death-and-fifth; bikkurim cancels the carcass\'s arising-on-its-own. What remains shared is only: the liquid follows the substance.' },
      'ter|cham': { ok: true, why: 'Forged! Chametz cancels teruma\'s death-and-fifth; teruma cancels chametz\'s arising-on-its-own. The Gemara\'s own answer: teruma and one of these.' },
      'ter|carc': { ok: true, why: 'Forged! The carcass cancels teruma\'s death-and-fifth; teruma cancels the carcass\'s arising-on-its-own. The Gemara\'s own answer: teruma and one of these.' },
    };

    // ---------- Act III data ----------
    const LENS_CARDS = [
      {
        q: 'A non-priest drinks date honey, apple wine, or autumn-grape vinegar made from teruma (Mishna Terumot 11:2)',
        e: { v: 'Pays principal + a fifth', cls: 'red', why: 'Infer from it and again from it: as bikkurim covers all seven species, teruma\'s liquid-law covers these juices too — full teruma penalties.' },
        y: { v: 'Exempt from payment', cls: 'teal', why: 'Interpret in its own place: teruma\'s own liquids are wine and oil only. Other juices never take on the produce\'s status.' },
        ref: 'Chullin.120b.14', refLabel: '120b:14–17',
      },
      {
        q: 'Which beverages may be brought to the Temple as first fruits? (Mishna Terumot 11:3)',
        e: { v: 'Juice of any of the seven species', cls: 'amber', why: 'The full source case travels: bikkurim liquid = bikkurim, for every species of the seven.' },
        y: { v: 'Only wine and oil', cls: 'teal', why: 'The derivation runs back through teruma, whose own liquids are wine and oil — so even bikkurim beverages stop there. This is the mishna\'s ruling.' },
        ref: 'Chullin.120b.18', refLabel: '120b:18–19',
      },
      {
        q: 'Lashes for drinking juice squeezed from orla fruit (Mishna Terumot 11:3)',
        e: { v: 'Broader liability', cls: 'amber', why: 'On his method the liquid of any orla fruit could carry the fruit\'s own status.' },
        y: { v: 'Only what flows from olives and grapes', cls: 'teal', why: 'In its own place: wine and oil alone are flogged as the fruit itself — the mishna again follows Rabbi Yehoshua.' },
        ref: 'Chullin.120b.20', refLabel: '120b:20–21',
      },
    ];

    // ---------- state ----------
    let score = 0, answered = 0, forgeSolved = false;
    const TOTAL = BENCH.length + FORGE.length;
    const scoreEl = document.getElementById('score');
    function bump(firstTry) { if (firstTry) score++; answered++; scoreEl.textContent = `${score} / ${TOTAL}`; maybeFinale(); }

    // ---------- Act I render ----------
    const benchEl = document.getElementById('bench');
    BENCH.forEach((r, i) => {
      const card = document.createElement('div');
      card.className = 'mb-4 rounded-2xl border border-[#1e3a30] bg-[#0c1a15] p-4';
      card.innerHTML = `
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
          <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] ${C.mute}">specimen ${i + 1} of ${BENCH.length}</p>
          <p class="frank text-lg font-bold ${C.amber}" dir="rtl" lang="he">${r.he}</p>
        </div>
        <h3 class="fraunces mt-0.5 text-lg font-bold ${C.text}">${r.name}</h3>
        <div class="mt-2 flex flex-col items-center gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-start">
          <div class="flask-wrap">${flaskSVG(r.pre)}</div>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed ${C.dim}">${r.scenario}</p>
            <button class="proc-btn mt-3 rounded-xl border border-[#5ecfb4]/50 bg-[#10241d] px-4 py-2 text-sm font-bold ${C.teal} hover:bg-[#153029]">${r.process}</button>
            <div class="opts mt-3 hidden space-y-2"></div>
            <div class="reveal mt-3 hidden rounded-xl border border-[#1e3a30] bg-[#08120e] p-3 text-sm leading-relaxed ${C.dim}" aria-live="polite"></div>
          </div>
        </div>`;
      benchEl.appendChild(card);

      const procBtn = card.querySelector('.proc-btn');
      const optsEl = card.querySelector('.opts');
      const revealEl = card.querySelector('.reveal');
      let tried = false, done = false;

      procBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        setFlask(card.querySelector('.flask-wrap'), r.post);
        procBtn.disabled = true;
        procBtn.className = `proc-btn mt-3 rounded-xl border border-[#1e3a30] bg-[#0c1a15] px-4 py-2 text-sm ${C.mute}`;
        optsEl.classList.remove('hidden');
        if (optsEl.childElementCount === 0) {
          r.options.forEach((o, oi) => {
            const b = document.createElement('button');
            b.className = `verdict-btn block w-full rounded-xl border border-[#1e3a30] bg-[#0e1f19] px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm ${C.dim} hover:border-[#e8ae3c]/60`;
            b.textContent = o;
            b.addEventListener('click', () => {
              if (done) return;
              if (oi === r.correct) {
                done = true;
                b.className = `verdict-btn block w-full rounded-xl border border-[#e8ae3c] bg-[#17211a] px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm font-bold ${C.amber}`;
                revealEl.classList.remove('hidden');
                revealEl.innerHTML = `${r.reveal} <span class="whitespace-nowrap">— ${sef(r.ref, r.refLabel)}</span>`;
                bump(!tried);
              } else {
                tried = true;
                b.disabled = true;
                b.className = `verdict-btn block w-full rounded-xl border border-[#e2604f]/60 bg-[#1c1210] px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm line-through ${C.mute}`;
              }
            });
            optsEl.appendChild(b);
          });
        }
      });
    });

    // ---------- Act II render ----------
    const forgeEl = document.getElementById('forge');
    FORGE.forEach((r, i) => {
      const card = document.createElement('div');
      card.className = 'mb-4 rounded-2xl border border-[#1e3a30] bg-[#0c1a15] p-4';
      card.innerHTML = `
        <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] ${C.mute}">attempt ${i + 1} of ${FORGE.length}</p>
        <h3 class="fraunces mt-0.5 text-lg font-bold ${C.text}">${r.title}</h3>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed ${C.dim}">${r.setup}</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide ${C.teal}">what blocks it?</p>
        <div class="opts mt-2 space-y-2"></div>
        <div class="reveal mt-3 hidden rounded-xl border border-[#1e3a30] bg-[#08120e] p-3 text-sm leading-relaxed ${C.dim}" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      forgeEl.appendChild(card);
      const optsEl = card.querySelector('.opts');
      const revealEl = card.querySelector('.reveal');
      let tried = false, done = false;
      r.options.forEach((o, oi) => {
        const b = document.createElement('button');
        b.className = `verdict-btn block w-full rounded-xl border border-[#1e3a30] bg-[#0e1f19] px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm ${C.dim} hover:border-[#5ecfb4]/60`;
        b.textContent = o;
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          if (done) return;
          if (oi === r.correct) {
            done = true;
            b.className = `verdict-btn block w-full rounded-xl border border-[#5ecfb4] bg-[#10241d] px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm font-bold ${C.teal}`;
            revealEl.classList.remove('hidden');
            revealEl.innerHTML = `${r.reveal} <span class="whitespace-nowrap">— ${sef(r.ref, r.refLabel)}</span>`;
            bump(!tried);
          } else {
            tried = true; b.disabled = true;
            b.className = `verdict-btn block w-full rounded-xl border border-[#e2604f]/60 bg-[#1c1210] px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm line-through ${C.mute}`;
          }
        });
        optsEl.appendChild(b);
      });
    });

    // Forge finale: the hekdesh pair
    const pairCard = document.createElement('div');
    pairCard.className = 'mb-4 rounded-2xl border border-[#e8ae3c]/40 bg-[#0c1a15] p-4';
    pairCard.innerHTML = `
      <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] ${C.amber}">the forge's last fire</p>
      <h3 class="fraunces mt-0.5 text-lg font-bold ${C.text}">Forge a source for consecrated produce</h3>
      <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed ${C.dim}">
        Hekdesh liquid must be forbidden like the produce — but hekdesh only exists once a person
        consecrates it, so the "arises on its own" family can't carry it alone. The Gemara already
        burned through the singles: <b class="${C.text}">bikkurim alone</b> is blocked (it demands
        the recitation "My father was a wandering Aramean" and placement in the Temple);
        <b class="${C.text}">teruma alone</b> is blocked (death at the hand of Heaven + the added
        fifth). Pick the <b class="${C.amber}">pair</b> whose stringencies cancel out.
      </p>
      <div class="pair-cards mt-3 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2"></div>
      <button class="forge-go mt-3 w-full rounded-xl border border-[#e8ae3c]/60 bg-[#17211a] px-4 py-2 text-sm font-bold ${C.amber} disabled:opacity-40" disabled>🔨 Strike the forge</button>
      <div class="reveal mt-3 hidden rounded-xl border border-[#1e3a30] bg-[#08120e] p-3 text-sm leading-relaxed ${C.dim}" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
    forgeEl.appendChild(pairCard);

    const picked = new Set();
    const pairWrap = pairCard.querySelector('.pair-cards');
    const goBtn = pairCard.querySelector('.forge-go');
    const pairReveal = pairCard.querySelector('.reveal');
    PAIR_CARDS.forEach((p) => {
      const b = document.createElement('button');
      b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');
      b.className = `pairbtn rounded-xl border border-[#1e3a30] bg-[#0e1f19] px-3 py-2.5 text-left transition`;
      b.innerHTML = `<span class="block text-sm font-bold ${C.text}">${p.name} <span class="frank ${C.amber}" dir="rtl" lang="he">${p.he}</span></span>
        <span class="block text-[11px] ${C.mute}">${p.note}</span>`;
      b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (picked.has(p.id)) { picked.delete(p.id); b.style.borderColor = ''; b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false'); }
        else if (picked.size < 2) { picked.add(p.id); b.style.borderColor = '#e8ae3c'; b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true'); }
        goBtn.disabled = picked.size !== 2;
      });
      pairWrap.appendChild(b);
    });
    goBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const key = ['bik', 'ter', 'cham', 'carc'].filter((id) => picked.has(id)).join('|');
      const v = PAIR_VERDICTS[key];
      pairReveal.classList.remove('hidden');
      pairReveal.innerHTML = `${v.ok ? `<b class="${C.amber}">` : `<b class="${C.red}">`}${v.ok ? '⚒️ It holds.' : 'It shatters.'}</b> ${v.why}
        <span class="whitespace-nowrap">— ${sef('Chullin.120b.13', 'Chullin 120b:3–13')}</span>`;
      if (v.ok && !forgeSolved) { forgeSolved = true; maybeFinale(); }
    });

    // ---------- Act III render ----------
    const lensCardsEl = document.getElementById('lens-cards');
    const tabE = document.getElementById('lens-e'), tabY = document.getElementById('lens-y');
    const VCLS = { red: C.red, teal: C.teal, amber: C.amber };
    function renderLens(mode) {
      tabE.setAttribute('aria-selected', mode === 'e');
      tabY.setAttribute('aria-selected', mode === 'y');
      lensCardsEl.innerHTML = LENS_CARDS.map((c) => {
        const v = c[mode];
        return `<div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#1e3a30] bg-[#0c1a15] p-4">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold leading-snug ${C.text}">${c.q}</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-base font-bold ${VCLS[v.cls]}">${v.v}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed ${C.dim}">${v.why}
            <span class="whitespace-nowrap">— ${sef(c.ref, c.refLabel)}</span></p>
        </div>`;
      }).join('');
    }
    tabE.addEventListener('click', () => renderLens('e'));
    tabY.addEventListener('click', () => renderLens('y'));
    renderLens('y');

    // ---------- finale ----------
    function maybeFinale() {
      if (answered < TOTAL || !forgeSolved) return;
      const f = document.getElementById('finale');
      let grade, note;
      if (score >= 12) { grade = '🍷 Wine of the first fruits', note = 'Fit to be brought to the Temple — Rabbi Yosei himself would accept your derivations.'; }
      else if (score >= 9) { grade = '🍯 Date honey', note = 'Sweet and nearly teruma — though Rabbi Eliezer would still charge you the added fifth.'; }
      else if (score >= 5) { grade = '🫗 Autumn-grape vinegar', note = 'Stunted grapes, sharp finish. Rabbi Yehoshua exempts you; take the win and review the daf.'; }
      else { grade = '☀️ Melted in the sun', note = 'It rotted before it melted — unfit for consumption, but also exempt from all liability. Run the bench again.'; }
      f.classList.remove('hidden');
      f.innerHTML = `
        <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.25em] ${C.mute}">your distillate</p>
        <p class="fraunces mt-2 text-2xl font-black ${C.amber}">${grade}</p>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-2 max-w-md text-sm leading-relaxed ${C.dim}">${note}</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm ${C.text}">${score} of ${TOTAL} verdicts stamped on the first try — and the hekdesh derivation forged.</p>`;
      const reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      f.scrollIntoView({ behavior: reduce ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'center' });
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
